.TH "HED-AISHELL" "1" "2026-08-11" "hed v1.19.0" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-aishell \- Opens an AI assistant (Claude Code, Copilot, etc.)
in a dedicated tmux pane and lets you push text into it from the editor.
.PP
Opens an AI assistant (Claude Code, Copilot, etc.)
in a dedicated tmux pane and lets you push text into it from the editor.
.PP
Piggybacks on the \f[CR]tmux\f[R] plugin\[cq]s named\-pane registry, so
the lifecycle (create on first toggle, hide via \f[CR]break\-pane\f[R],
show via \f[CR]join\-pane\f[R], kill) is identical to the runner pane
\[em] just with your configured command instead of a shell.
.SH Configuration
Set the spawn command in \f[CR]src/config.h\f[R] (or your custom config)
before loading the plugin:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]/* Default is \[dq]claude\[dq] \[em] change to use something else: */\f[R]
aishell_set_spawn_cmd(\[dq]copilot\[dq]);
aishell_set_spawn_cmd(\[dq]aider\[dq]);
aishell_set_spawn_cmd(\[dq]windsurf\[dq]);
.EE
.SH Commands
